Hi Elena, I re-ran the coverage query and found something that changes the gap number.

**Finding:** Grouping the 1284 items with `found in taxon` (P703) = Arabidopsis thaliana (Q158695) by `instance of` (P31) shows ~271 are not chemicals:

| Class | Count |
|---|---|
| class of protein-containing complexes (Q107509287) | 228 |
| gene (Q7187) | 28 |
| chromosome (Q37748) | 7 |
| protein (Q8054) | 5 |
| MeSH single protein entry (Q101563126) | 1 |
| no P31 at all | 3 |

Restricting to chemical classes gives **1013 chemicals, of which 118 (11.6%) link to a WikiPathways pathway**, instead of 118/1284 = 9.2%. The gap is still ~88%, but the denominator should be filtered by chemical class.

Also: only 2 of the 1013 are `instance of` "chemical compound" (Q11173); 804 are "type of chemical entity" (Q113145171), which supports the class-inconsistency finding.

**Query (could be added as queries/03):**
```sparql
SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?c) AS ?chemicalsTotal)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?cPathway) AS ?chemicalsWithPathway)
WHERE {
  VALUES ?class { wd:Q113145171 wd:Q59199015 wd:Q15711994 wd:Q11173 wd:Q56256173 }
  ?c wdt:P703 wd:Q158695 ;
     wdt:P31 ?class .
  OPTIONAL {
    ?p wdt:P527 ?c ;
       wdt:P2410 ?wp .
    BIND(?c AS ?cPathway)
  }
}
```
